-- Playbook ve-vouch-points: the decision Sean locked 2026-11-15 (talked through with V, built by Logan the same day). Safe to run twice.
insert into playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-vouch-points', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan Russell', $b$ve-vouch-points: LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-15 ("Let's lock it in"). Asked while building Nearectory's vouching system: is one vouch per business better than voting once a day? 1) Vouches decide rankings: one vote per member per business, kept until they take it back (Sean: "make it so somebody can unvote as well... I might make a mistake and I want to be able to undo it"); the count is the number of people (Sean: "only count my vote once for each listing that I voted for"). LIVE same day: ve-votes v12 (one per member, `unvote`, a repeat is 409 already_voted), trigger fn_listing_vote_count counts distinct members, every listing backfilled (884 votes became 711 people), Undo my vote in the Voted window (public/ve-votes.js, directory/listing.html), "vote every day" copy removed. 2) The daily habit is earning points to give (Sean: "some sort of activity that gets them coming back daily... donate points so that these businesses can use it for our different marketing services"): members earn points daily (check-ins, the Daily Pulse, Bounties, a question a day) and give them to businesses; businesses spend given points on Vegans Explore's own promotion (Pulse feature, social feature, house ad slot, Guide spotlight), never LESARUSS.ai's paid services and never cash. 3) Owners and staff may give to their own business (Sean: "They earn the points. It'd be investing in their own business"); the public "supported by N members" counts outside supporters only, the business sees its own share on its dashboard. 4) Guardrails: no cash value, a monthly cap per business, abuse watch on point farming; points never move rankings. Open, to build next: what each promotion costs in points and the monthly cap, the give flow on the listing and dashboard, the business's points wallet and redemption, the outside-supporter count, yearly vouch renewal (suggested, not locked), and the same model on Nearectory.$b$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from playbook_records where slug = 've-vouch-points' and body like 've-vouch-points: LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-15%');
